        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "cfd80e2e-2ac2-51da-9407-f15c6ec0afa5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Helen Jonas-Rosenzweig, Amon Göth\n- Places: Kraków-Płaszów concentration camp, Płaszów, German-occupied Poland\n- Roles: Holocaust survivor, SS-Hauptsturmführer, camp commandant, maid\n- Events: World War II, the Holocaust\n\nFacts:\n- Helen Jonas-Rosenzweig was born Helena Sternlicht on 25 April 1925.\n- Amon Göth was born on 11 December 1908 and died on 13 September 1946.\n- During World War II, Helen Jonas-Rosenzweig was interned at the Kraków-Płaszów concentration camp as a Holocaust survivor and was forced to work there as a maid for camp commandant Amon Göth.\n- During World War II, Amon Göth was an Austrian SS-Hauptsturmführer and served as commandant of the Kraków-Płaszów concentration camp in Płaszów, German-occupied Poland, for most of the camp's existence.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
